Now let me check what the OPENPGP mode implementation looks like to understand the security implications of this change.

```json
{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "search_code",
  "arguments": {
    "query": "MODE_OPENPGP",
    "max_results": 10
  },
  "reason": "Find the OPENPGP mode implementation to understand the security context"
}
```

Let me check the blockalgo module to understand how OPENPGP mode works.

```json
{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "search_code",
  "arguments": {
    "query": "MODE_OPENPGP",
    "path": "lib/Crypto/Cipher/blockalgo.py",
    "max_results": 5
  },
  "reason": "Find the OPENPGP mode implementation in blockalgo to understand the security implications"
}
```

Let me read the OPENPGP implementation in blockalgo to understand the security implications.

```json
{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "read_file",
  "arguments": {
    "path": "lib/Crypto/Cipher/blockalgo.py",
    "start_line": 200,
    "end_line": 300
  },
  "reason": "Read the OPENPGP mode implementation to understand how it handles encryption/decryption"
}
```

Now let me check how the encrypted IV is handled in the OPENPGP mode initialization.

```json
{
  "type": "tool",
  "tool": "read_file",
  "arguments": {
    "path": "lib/Crypto/Cipher/blockalgo.py",
    "start_line": 100,
    "end_line": 200
  },
  "reason": "Check how OPENPGP mode handles IV initialization and the encrypted IV"
}
```
